{
  "name": "noncanonical-key-rendering-malformed",
  "description": "#116: every key-bearing field must be the key's canonical rendering. Genesis admits A, B and passkey P. Ops naming a whitespace-padded or uppercase-hex rendering of a key — as dev (A, and passkey P), as by (A signing), or as usr (genesis) — are malformed and uncitable, and an op citing one is bad_prev. So the padded add of A is not a second member and does not raise the high-water: N stays 2 (A, B), k is 1, and A's single-signature remove of B is effective",
